# ETSU Marketplace 
(Palwasha Newell & Nathanael Wolfe)

## Project Proposal

### 1. Application Overview

ETSU Marketplace is a university-exclusive web-based marketplace that allows verified students to buy, sell, and exchange items, as well as post and browse lease takeover requests. The platform is restricted to university students through email authentication to ensure a safe and trusted campus environment.

The purpose of this application is to:
- Provide a safe marketplace restricted to university students
- Reduce scams common on public marketplaces
- Centralize item sales and lease takeover opportunities for campus life

This application is built using ASP.NET Core MVC and follows best practices in full-stack web development as required by the course guidelines.

---

### 2. Target Users

**Primary Users:**
- University Students

**Secondary Users:**
- Administrators (moderation only)

---

### 3. Core Functionalities (User Stories Summary)

#### Authentication & Access Control
- Students can register using their university email address
- Students can log in to access marketplace features
- Access is restricted to verified university students only

#### Item Listings
- Students can create listings with:
  - Title
  - Description
  - Price
  - Images
- Students can edit their own listings
- Students can delete their own listings
- Students can view all active listings
- Students can search listings
- Students can filter listings by category
- Students can view seller profiles
- Students can contact sellers through internal messaging

#### Lease Takeover Listings
- Students can create lease takeover requests with:
  - Title
  - Description
  - Monthly rent
  - Images
- Students can edit lease takeover requests
- Students can delete lease takeover requests
- Students can filter lease takeover listings
- Students can contact lease posters via messaging

#### Messaging System
- Students can send messages to other students
- Messages can be related to a specific listing
- Students can receive messages from other students

---

### 4. Data Model Overview

The system includes the following main entities:
- ApplicationUser
- Listing
- LeaseTakeover
- Category
- ListingCategory (many-to-many bridge table)
- ListingImage
- Message

**Many-to-Many Relationship:**
- A Listing can belong to multiple Categories
- A Category can have multiple Listings
- Implemented using the ListingCategory junction table

