## Project Overview
ETSU Marketplace is a full-stack ASP.NET Core MVC web application designed to allow users to create, browse, and manage marketplace listings. The platform enables users to buy, sell, and lease items while interacting with other users through messaging and personalized features such as favorites.

The application demonstrates core web development concepts including MVC architecture, RESTful APIs, database design, authentication, and client-side interactivity. This project demonstrates a complete full-stack application integrating backend, frontend, and real-time communication technologies.

---

## Features
- User registration and authentication
- Full CRRUD (Create, Read, Read All, Update, Delete) operations for listings
- Create, view, update, and delete listings (items and leases)
- Search and filter listings
- Favorite/unfavorite listings
- Real-time messaging between users (SignalR)
- Categorization of listings
- Responsive UI for desktop and mobile devices

---

## Technologies Used
- ASP.NET Core MVC
- Entity Framework Core
- SQLite (or your database)
- JavaScript (AJAX, Fetch API, SignalR)
- Bootstrap (responsive design)
- HTML5 / CSS3

---

## System Architecture

![System Architecture](docs/ArchDesign.png)

The application follows the ASP.NET Core MVC architecture pattern. Controllers handle user requests, services manage business logic, and Entity Framework Core manages data persistence. A RESTful API is integrated to support asynchronous operations and client-side interactions.

---

## Data Model

![Entity Relationship Diagram](docs/ERD.png)

The data model consists of multiple interconnected entities including users, listings, categories, messages, and favorites. Relationships include one-to-many and many-to-many associations, implemented using Entity Framework Core. These relationships allow flexible connections such as users favoriting listings and listings belonging to multiple categories.

---

## API Endpoints

The application provides a RESTful API to support data operations and asynchronous features. The API follows REST principles and uses standard HTTP methods including GET, POST, PUT, and DELETE.

### Item Listings
- `GET /api/ItemAPI`
- `GET /api/ItemAPI/{id}`
- `POST /api/ItemAPI`
- `PUT /api/ItemAPI/{id}`
- `DELETE /api/ItemAPI/{id}`

### Lease Listings
- `GET /api/LeaseAPI`
- `GET /api/LeaseAPI/{id}`
- `POST /api/LeaseAPI`
- `PUT /api/LeaseAPI/{id}`
- `DELETE /api/LeaseAPI/{id}`

---

## AJAX and Asynchronous Features

- Favoriting listings updates instantly without reloading the page
- Live search dynamically filters listings using API calls
- SignalR is used for real-time messaging between users

